            0.254,
            0.368,
            0.883,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "3. You have learnt that different conditions are required for seed germination. How can we use this knowledge for proper storage of grains and pulses?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.433,
            0.885,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "4. You have learnt that a tail is present in a tadpole but it disappears as it grows into a frog. What is the advantage of having a tail in the tadpole stage?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.498,
            0.883,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": "5. Charan says that a wooden log is non-living as it cannot move. Charu counters it by saying that it is living because it is made of wood obtained from trees. Give your arguments in favour or against the two statements given by Charan and Charu."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
